tps://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400316.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2015","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400315.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2014","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400314.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2013","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/532440/5324400313.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2012","url":"https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/AR_MPSLTD_2011_2012_31122012122020.zip","source":"the data provider"}],"analysis":{"summary":"MPS Limited reported its strongest first quarter in history for Q1 FY27, with revenue reaching INR 224.24 crores and EBITDA increasing 53.0 percent to INR 76.96 crores. Management reaffirmed its guidance to comfortably cross INR 300 crores in EBITDA for FY27, viewing it as a floor rather than a ceiling. The company is actively driving a structural shift from effort-based billing toward outcomes-based revenue across its business segments. Additionally, management highlighted strong operational leverage, disciplined cost management, and ongoing integration and synergies from the Unbound Medicine acquisition. MPS Limited reported its strongest opening quarter in history for Q1 FY27, achieving record revenue of INR 22,424 Lakhs and an EBITDA margin of 34.32%.","themes":{"guidance":[{"claim":"Management reiterated its FY27 EBITDA guidance to comfortably cross INR 300 Crores.","quote":"FY27: TRACKING TO COMFORTBALY CROSS INR 300 CRORES IN EBITDA","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"The company expects to clear INR 300 Crores as a mark built bottom-up from each segment operating plan.","quote":"~21% three-year EBITDA CAGR (FY24 to FY27), built bottom-up from each segment operating plan","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"}],"demand_outlook":[{"claim":"Demand for AJE's newly launched Pre-Submission Peer Review has run well ahead of plan.","quote":"We launched Pre-Submission Peer Review in April, our first genuinely new service in more than two years, and demand has run well ahead of what we planned.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"Research Solutions revenue grew 7.6% year-over-year in Q4 to INR 120 crores.","quote":"Q4 reported revenue was INR 120 crores, up 7.6% year-over-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Education Q4 revenue reached INR 60 crores, up 30.5% year-over-year.","quote":"Q4 revenue reached INR 60 crores, up 30.5% year-over-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Corporate learning Q4 revenue grew 2.4% year-over-year to INR 25.5 crores.","quote":"Q4 revenue grew 2.4% year-over-year to INR 25.5 crores, the first positive print of the year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"capex_expansion":[{"claim":"Unbound Medicine acquisition closed on February 9, 2026.","quote":"Third, the Unbound Medicine acquisition, which closed on February 9, 2026.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"margins_costs":[{"claim":"Reported revenue for the quarter was INR 224.24 crores, up 20.4 percent year over year.","quote":"Reported revenue for the quarter was INR 224.24 crores, up 20.4 percent over the same quarter last year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"EBITDA was INR 76.96 crores, up 53.0 percent, with the EBITDA margin expanding to 34.3 percent.","quote":"EBITDA was INR 76.96 crores, up 53.0 percent, with the EBITDA margin expanding to 34.3 percent from 27.0 percent a year ago.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"Profit after tax grew 43.0 percent to INR 50.39 crores and basic EPS came in at INR 29.70.","quote":"Profit after tax grew 43.0 percent to INR 50.39 crores, and basic EPS came in at INR 29.70, an all-time Q1 high, up from INR 20.78.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"Excluding AJE, underlying revenue grew 28.4 percent to INR 198.47 crores and EBITDA grew 50.5 percent.","quote":"Strip out AJE, which is resetting by design and which Christine will speak to, and the underlying business grew faster still: revenue up 28.4 percent to INR 198.47 crores, EBITDA up 50.5 percent, and the margin expanding close to five points to 32.4 percent.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"EBITDA margin expanded by 6.06 points to 33.73% excluding AJE.","quote":"EBITDA margin expanded by 6.06 points to 33.73%","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Group EBITDA for FY26 was INR 236 crores with the EBITDA margin expanding to 30.7%.","quote":"EBITDA was INR 236 crores, up by 11.8%, with the EBITDA margin expanding to 30.7%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Profit after tax grew 16.3% to INR 173 crores for FY26.","quote":"Profit after tax grew 16.3% to INR 173 crores, and the basic EPS came in at INR 102.11, a Company record up 16.3% year-on-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"The Research segment EBITDA margin expanded 330 basis points to 39.9% for the full year.","quote":"The Research segment EBITDA margin expanded 330 basis points to 39.9% for the year, and Education delivered EBITDA growth of 42.6% year-over-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Q4 EBITDA grew 20.5% to INR 67.5 crores with margins expanding to 32.9%.","quote":"EBITDA grew 20.5% to INR 67.5 crores with the margins expanding to 32.9%, indicating operating leverage at work as revenue growth converted to margin expansion.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"Headcount in the corporate learning segment is down approximately 32% year-on-year.","quote":"Headcount in the segment is down approximately 32% year-on-year on a much sharper cost base.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"orders_capacity":[{"claim":"Client count rose across the company to 841 from 404 a year ago as Unbound's institutional subscribers were added.","quote":"and you can see it most clearly in our client count, which rose across the Company to 841 from 404 a year ago as Unbound's institutional subscribers came onto our books.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"Corporate learning closed Q4 with the strongest order book of FY26.","quote":"Q4 closed with the strongest order book of FY'26.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"capital_allocation":[{"claim":"Total cash and cash equivalents stood at INR 138.02 crores as of 30 June against borrowings of INR 37.63 crores.","quote":"Total cash and cash equivalents stood at INR 138.02 crores as of 30 June, against borrowings of INR 37.63 crores relating to the facility we drew for the Unbound Medicine acquisition.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf"},{"claim":"Debtors DSO improved QoQ to 45 days from 51 days.","quote":"DSO improved QoQ to 45 days from 51 days, reflecting enhanced collection efficiency and tighter working capital management","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf"},{"claim":"Total cash and cash equivalents stood at INR 113.75 crores as of March 31, 2026, with borrowings of INR 40.25 crores for Unbound Medicine.","quote":"On the balance sheet, total cash and cash equivalents stood at INR 113.75 crores as of 31 March 26, with borrowings of INR 40.25 crores relating to the facility drawn for the acquisition of Unbound Medicine.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"},{"claim":"The Board chose not to recommend a final dividend for FY26 due to capital deployment into the Unbound Medicine acquisition and pipeline opportunities.","quote":"Over FY’26, the Board has chosen not to recommend a final dividend. The reason is straightforward. We've deployed capital into the Unbound Medicine acquisition in February, we're carrying a hyperactive M&A pipeline, and the deployment opportunity in front of us exceeds the cash in hand.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=19ba1493-4998-44d2-a6a5-2cd9b7f7615f.pdf"}],"risks_headwinds":[]},"management_commitments":[{"claim":"Management expects the company to comfortably cross INR 300 crores in EBITDA in FY27.","quote":"We continue to expect the Company to comfortably cross INR 300 crores in EBITDA in FY'27.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=24e4d51b-25c9-46ec-87e3-ec0ebb26767e.pdf","timeframe":"FY27"},{"claim":"Management reiterated its FY27 EBITDA guidance to comfortably cross INR 300 Crores.","quote":"FY27: TRACKING TO COMFORTBALY CROSS INR 300 CRORES IN EBITDA","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=0f2c9a6d-7a46-44ae-a149-b68925f2e76b.pdf","timeframe":"FY27"}],"coverage":{"docs_analysed":3,"kinds":["concall_transcript","concall_ppt"]}},"_meta":{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash","grounded":true,"facts_kept":25,"facts_dropped_ungrounded":9,"note":"Facts are verbatim-grounded against the company's own documents; claims whose quote was not found were dropped."}}